A||N||9||chris6878||Guage/Dash lights?||||5||
Z||000000||chris6878||03-30-2000||11:12 AM||||Well.. they used to work fine when i first go the car on the road.. then they went off for few days and then mysteriously came back..  now they havent came on in  while.. would this be the headlight switch on the dash? since it has controls to dim or brighthen the dash lights?     <P>TIA<BR>Chris||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||03-30-2000||11:36 AM||||I would check out the dimmer switch first. They can go bad.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||03-30-2000||12:11 PM||||Under the driver's side of the dash very close to the console, is an assembly that has a transistor (silver diamond shaped thing) mounted in the middle. On the back of this transistor are two metal pins that poke through the rest of the assembly into two sockets. It's usually a bad connection at those sockets. Don't clean off the white stuff, from the back of the transistor. It's thermal compound. Helps transfer the heat from the transistor into the mount. Don't lose the clear "gasket". It's an insulator. <BR>The way this works is... The knob on the dash varies the voltage (low current) to the transistor. The transistor, in turn, varies the voltage (high current) to the dash lights. <BR>GM charges around $30 for the assembly. This fix is free.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||chris6878||03-30-2000||01:40 PM||||Thanks, I will check it out soon as i get home this evening....  it will be nice to see my guages once again after dark...||||reg||14
Z||000004||Raydar||03-30-2000||03:51 PM||||Chris,<BR>The entire assembly can be removed. Only a screw or two hold it in. One three-wire electrical connector. <BR>Once you have it out, two hex screws hold the transistor to the heatsink assembly.||||reg||1
Z||000005||chris6878||03-30-2000||04:27 PM||||thanks.. i'll will let ya know this fixes it...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   later..<P>chris||||reg||1
